Embedded React: a conic gradient seen through a View's border ring.

Modified from Embedded React (Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Cory Lamming) at the
revision pinned in dependencies.lock.json, after the patches listed before this
one there. Changed files: engine/include/er_scene.h,
engine/scene/er_node_internal.h, engine/scene/compositor.c,
engine/animation/animation.c, engine/rendering/border_sweep.c,
engine/rendering/border_sweep.h, bridges/quickjs/native_ui_bridge.c,
bridges/quickjs/js/src/embedded-react/index.d.ts and
engine/tests/rendering/test_border_sweep.c. Proposed upstream, with the other
border ring patches, as pull request #325.

The rotating-gradient border (a conic gradient turning behind the card, masked
to its border) is the classic focus-ring shimmer. The View style
borderGradient {type: 'conic', width, angle, stops} draws a conic gradient,
CSS conic-gradient style (0 degrees up, clockwise, up to 6 straight-alpha
stops), only inside the anti-aliased rounded ring `width` px thick along the
box's edge, over the content. borderGradientAngle sets the start angle and
animates on the native driver; an angle-only change damages the ring's edge
bands, like the border sweep it shares its rasteriser with.

